    "title": "911 call shed light on moments leading up to officer-involved shooting in Clermont County - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Daniel Zivian, WKRC ,\n1 hours ago CLERMONT COUNTY, Ohio (WKRC) - Union Township police have released the 911 call from an officer-involved shooting on Monday, where 37-year-old Thomas Noble was shot by an officer after a \"hostage situation\" escalated. The call, placed by Noble's mother just before 9 p.m., reveals the tense moments leading up to... Read full article\nRead in NewsBreak",
